1
00:03:31,875 --> 00:03:37,875
They stole his mind. Now, he wants it back.

2
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:09,750
Total Recall is a action, adventure, science
fiction film directed by Paul Verhoeven.

3
00:10:35,625 --> 00:10:41,625
Construction worker Douglas Quaid's obsession with the planet Mars leads
him to visit Recall, a company that manufactures memories.

4
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:13,500
When his memory implant goes wrong, Doug can no
longer be sure what is and isn't reality.

5
00:17:39,375 --> 00:17:45,375
Douglas Quaid / Hauser, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

6
00:21:11,250 --> 00:21:17,250
Melina, played by Rachel Ticotin.

7
00:24:43,125 --> 00:24:49,125
Lori Quaid, played by Sharon Stone.

8
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Vilos Cohaagen, played by Ronny Cox.

9
00:31:46,875 --> 00:31:52,875
Richter, played by Michael Ironside.

10
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:24,750
George / Kuato, played by Marshall Bell.

11
00:38:50,625 --> 00:38:56,625
Total Recall is a 1990 American science fiction action film directed by Paul Verhoeven,
with a screenplay by Ronald Shusett, Dan O'Bannon, and Gary Goldman.

12
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:28,500
The film stars Arnold Schwarzenegger, Rachel Ticotin,
Sharon Stone, Ronny Cox, and Michael Ironside.

13
00:45:54,375 --> 00:46:00,375
Based on the 1966 short story "We Can Remember It
for You Wholesale" by Philip K.

14
00:49:26,250 --> 00:49:32,250
Dick, Total Recall tells the story of Douglas Quaid (Schwarzenegger), a construction
worker who receives an implanted memory of a fantastical adventure on Mars.

15
00:52:58,125 --> 00:53:04,125
He subsequently finds his adventure occurring in reality as agents of a shadow organization try to prevent him from recovering memories
of his past as a Martian secret agent aiming to stop the tyrannical regime of the planet's dictator Vilos Cohaagen (Cox).

16
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Shusett bought the rights to Dick's short story in 1974
and developed a script with O'Bannon.

17
01:00:01,875 --> 01:00:07,875
Although considered promising, the ambitious scope kept the project in development hell at multiple studios over
sixteen years, seeing forty script drafts, seven different directors, and multiple actors cast as Quaid.

18
01:03:33,750 --> 01:03:39,750
Total Recall eventually entered the early stages of filming in 1987 under the De
Laurentiis Entertainment Group shortly before its bankruptcy.

19
01:07:05,625 --> 01:07:11,625
Schwarzenegger, who had long held an interest in the project but had been dismissed as inappropriate for the lead
role, convinced Carolco Pictures to purchase the rights and develop the film with him as the star.

20
01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:43,500
On an estimated $48–80 million budget (making it one of the most expensive films made in its time),
filming took place on expansive sets at Estudios Churubusco in Mexico over six months.

21
01:14:09,375 --> 01:14:15,375
Cast and crew experienced numerous injuries and illnesses during filming.

22
01:17:41,250 --> 01:17:47,250
Total Recall was anticipated to be one of the year's most successful films.

23
01:21:13,125 --> 01:21:19,125
On its release, the film earned approximately $261.4 million worldwide,
making it the fifth-highest-grossing film of the year.

24
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
Its critical reception was mixed, with reviewers praising its themes of identity and
questioning reality, but criticizing content perceived as vulgar and violent.

25
01:28:16,875 --> 01:28:22,875
The practical special effects were well received, earning the film an Academy Award, and
the score by Jerry Goldsmith has been praised as one of his best works.

26
01:31:48,750 --> 01:31:54,750
Since its release, Total Recall has been praised for its ambiguous ending positing whether Quaid's adventures are
real or a fantasy, and it has also been analyzed for themes of authoritarianism and colonialism.

27
01:35:20,625 --> 01:35:26,625
Retrospective reviews have called it one of Schwarzenegger's best films and
placed it among the best science fiction films ever made.

28
01:38:52,500 --> 01:38:58,500
Alongside comic books and video games, Total Recall has been adapted
into the 1999 television series Total Recall 2070.

29
01:42:24,375 --> 01:42:30,375
An early attempt at a sequel, based on Dick's The Minority Report, became the 2002 standalone film Minority
Report, while a 2012 remake, also titled Total Recall, failed to replicate the success of the original.

30
01:45:56,250 --> 01:46:02,250
The film explores themes of double life, planet mars,
based on novel or book, oxygen, resistance.

31
01:49:28,125 --> 01:49:34,125
The tone is thought_provoking.
